+// ---------- Worker threads translate the pieces (DM_NVN_PAR_WORKERS, parallel translation P3c slice C3) ----------
+// Included once at the end of nvn_mtl.m, after nvn_walk.inc and nvn_accum.inc. DM_NVN_PAR=1 and DM_NVN_PAR_WORKERS=K (1..4; 0, the default, keeps the one-thread pieces): K threads,
+// made at the first submission with planned cuts, translate the pieces of one submission at the same time; the replay thread commits them in piece order.
+//
+// Flow of a submission with n planned pieces (cuts g_pcp[0..n-2], pcw_plan):
+//   mtl_sub_index (replay thread): the walk plans the cuts; pcx_start decides per piece k >= 1 where it runs and queues the workers' pieces in order. A piece runs on the replay
+//     thread instead (in order, at its turn in pcx_finish) when the walk cannot give its start or its reads: it starts after a counter-value render condition (g_rc_skip is read from
+//     the counters at translation), it holds one (rc_value reads reports an earlier piece may still be writing), or the MetalFX upscaler chain is on and a dispatch came before
+//     it in the submission (g_upc_*). Once one piece runs on the replay thread every later one does too (each may read what that one sets).
+//   Piece 0: the replay thread translates it as before (mtl_exec); at its planned cut pc_cut ends and commits it (pc_end) and sets g_pcx_stop: mtl_exec unwinds, and the
+//     host's later mtl_exec calls of this submission return at once.
+//   A worker's piece (pcx_run): its own allocator (alloc_pick, fenced with the submission's fence) and command buffer, encoded directly (g_rec_off, also with
+//     DM_NVN_ENC_THREAD=1); the submission's tables copied in read-only (store look-ahead index, SET_RT / draw sequences, the walk's snapshots, the planned cuts); the start state
+//     from the walk's snapshot (pcw_restore), the memos cleared (pc_reset), the readers conservative (g_pc_cons), its lists empty (pca_begin). pcx_translate runs mtl_exec's own
+//     loop from the snapshot's OP_SET_RT: a called list's end continues at the snapshot's return addresses (g_ret), a handle's end at the next handle (h[hi + 1], g_rest). It stops at
+//     the next planned cut (pc_cut in role 2 closes the state there and sets g_pcx_stop) or at the submission's end (the last piece closes as mtl_sub_commit does). The worker ends
+//     the command buffer, waits for its uniform copies (ubc_wait) and hands back {command buffer, list record (pca_end_rec), its visibility slot, its end state}.
+//   mtl_sub_commit (replay thread, pcx_finish first): for k = 1..n-1 in order, waits for the worker's piece and commits it with pc_end's feedback handler (with the encode thread
