+// Included once at the end of nvn_mtl.m. When a submission's records are indexed (mtl_sub_index) the walk goes over the same records in mtl_exec's order (jumps, called lists,
+// the handles in turn) without translating, applies only the operations that change the SEED state into a shadow copy, and keeps a snapshot of it at each
+// render-target change (OP_SET_RT), the only place a piece is cut. A snapshot is the state when pc_end runs at that OP_SET_RT: before the operation's own target (a piece starting
+// there takes R.rt = the record, R.has_rt = 1), after the pending clears were flushed.
+// DM_NVN_PAR=1: the walk plans the submission's piece cuts (pcw_plan, see the Pieces block in nvn_mtl.m), and at each cut taken the next piece begins from the snapshot of its record
+// (pcw_restore, DM_NVN_PAR_RESTORE=1). DM_NVN_PAR_VERIFY=1: at each piece cut (pc_end, before the restore) the live SEED is compared with the snapshot of that record, field by
+// field, and the [parv] report line counts the cuts checked, the cuts with a difference and the fields that differed.
+// Both off (the default): mtl_sub_index makes one call that returns on two flags, pc_end one that returns on another (g_pcw_live, set only by a walk).
+//
+// Operations and the SEED they change (handlers in mtl_exec / state_op, nvn_mtl.m); W = the walk applies it, T = set by translation logic the walk cannot reproduce
+// (compared and reported on their own, not counted as a walk difference), - = no SEED change
+//   every operation        g_exec_seq           W  sdx_seq: +1 while the store look-ahead index matches (g_sdx_ok, g_sdx_op from mtl_sub_index)
+//   OP_END/JUMP/CALL       g_ret, g_ret_n       W  the call return stack; a cut can fall inside a called list
+//   OP_SET_RT              R.rt, R.has_rt       W  R.rt = the record; T where the record is taken by a hoisted clear pass, a deferred group or a fused pass (none at a safe cut,
+//                                                  but their R.rt can stand before one)
+//                          R.clear_*            W  zero after the operation's rp_flush / lc_push (a cut needs no landed clear); the values cc/cd/cs are compared only under their flags
