+// Mode bench (offline measure of the thread hand-over, no game): frame M, 25 submissions a frame shaped like the market log ([par0] 25.0 submissions a frame): 22 small ones of
+// 12 draws in 2 passes, and 3 large ones (650, 550, 450 draws, submissions 4, 12, 20) in passes of about 100 draws; every draw binds a texture handle (A and B in turn: the
+// arguments are encoded again) and sets a scissor, frame D's textured program; the large ones' draws cover the target with a fragment shader that loops (GPU work). No wait between submissions; one frame in flight (the next frame waits for the frame before).
+// Per variant: 50 warm-up frames, then MB_FRAMES timed; one more frame records the encoder records and the 6 targets, against today's (the first variant)
+enum { MB_NSUB = 25, MB_WARM = 50, MB_NV_MAX = 16 };
